WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:06.730
After this video you will be able to add a
well, a rain gauge,

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.770
a pond or any other water point as a station,
in five easy steps.

00:00:12.583 --> 00:00:14.743
Every station starts here.

00:00:14.863 --> 00:00:17.983
On your Home page, press My stations.

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:20.655
This is your list.

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:23.943
Press Add a station to register a new one.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.022
Adding a station takes five easy steps, shown
along the top.

00:00:29.142 --> 00:00:32.190
Nothing is saved until the very last button.

00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:35.585
Step one is the kind of station.

00:00:35.705 --> 00:00:42.641
Each picture is a kind of water point: a well,
a rain gauge, a pond, a river, and more.

00:00:42.761 --> 00:00:45.185
Press the one that matches yours.

00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:50.169
We will add an open well, so I press
Groundwater well.

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:52.881
The chosen picture gets a thick border.

00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.683
If yours is not listed, press Other.

00:00:56.803 --> 00:00:59.971
A new box asks what kind of station it is.

00:01:00.091 --> 00:01:05.419
It must be filled in, so OurWater asks for it
if you press Continue without it.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.562
Describe it in a few words, like Stepwell.

00:01:09.682 --> 00:01:11.770
The red message goes away.

00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:17.023
Ours is an open well, so I press Groundwater
well again.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.722
Press Continue.

00:01:19.842 --> 00:01:21.978
Step two is the name.

00:01:22.098 --> 00:01:25.098
Use a name your neighbours will recognise.

00:01:25.917 --> 00:01:28.293
I type Ramesh's open well.

00:01:28.413 --> 00:01:31.605
This is the one box here that must be filled
in.

00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:35.129
Alternative ID is optional.

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:39.233
If a project already has a number for this
well, write it here.

00:01:39.353 --> 00:01:42.593
OurWater makes the station's own code for you.

00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:47.233
The remark box is for any note that will help
the next person.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.922
Press Continue.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:54.170
Step three is the place, and it puts your
station on the map.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:58.394
Latitude, longitude and country must be filled
in.

00:01:59.217 --> 00:02:02.889
If you are standing at the well, press Current
location.

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:06.465
Your device may ask permission to share where
you are.

00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:08.457
Say yes.

00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:14.011
Your position appears as two numbers, latitude
and longitude.

00:02:14.131 --> 00:02:16.843
OurWater also looks up the place.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.618
It fills in the country, state, village and
district where it can.

00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:26.122
Check them, and type over anything that is
wrong.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.782
You can also type the numbers yourself.

00:02:29.902 --> 00:02:32.398
Latitude is north or south.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.086
Longitude is east or west.

00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:38.653
Numbers that cannot be right are caught.

00:02:38.773 --> 00:02:42.373
Latitude must be between minus ninety and
ninety.

00:02:43.183 --> 00:02:45.175
The third way is the map.

00:02:45.295 --> 00:02:49.423
Press Select different location, and the map
comes into view.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.458
Tap the map where the well is.

00:02:52.578 --> 00:02:57.186
A blue dot lands there, and the two number
boxes fill in by themselves.

00:02:58.017 --> 00:03:00.417
Country must be chosen too.

00:03:00.537 --> 00:03:03.177
Select the box and start typing.

00:03:03.297 --> 00:03:05.913
A list shows the matching countries.

00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:08.589
Press India.

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:11.277
Always pick your country from the list.

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:18.371
State, village, district and postcode are optional,
but they help people find the station.

00:03:19.183 --> 00:03:21.055
Press Continue.

00:03:21.175 --> 00:03:23.359
Step four is the photo.

00:03:23.479 --> 00:03:26.119
Take photo opens your phone camera.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:29.767
Choose from device picks a picture you already
have.

00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:32.815
I choose a picture of the well.

00:03:32.935 --> 00:03:35.071
A small preview appears.

00:03:35.191 --> 00:03:37.543
Remove lets you pick another one.

00:03:37.663 --> 00:03:39.559
A photo is optional.

00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.255
Press Continue.

00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.679
Step five is the review.

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:47.391
Everything you typed is listed here.

00:03:47.511 --> 00:03:49.383
Read it through.

00:03:50.217 --> 00:03:54.345
If something is wrong, press Back, or press a
step at the top.

00:03:54.465 --> 00:03:56.649
Nothing you typed is lost.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.370
Organisation admins see one more question
here: Whose is this station?

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:07.146
Everyone else owns their own stations, so
there is nothing to answer.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.526
When it looks right, press Save monitoring
station.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.086
A green message says Station saved.

00:04:15.917 --> 00:04:18.965
OurWater opens the new station's page.

00:04:19.085 --> 00:04:24.365
Its buttons show it on the map, open its data
history, edit it, or delete it.

00:04:25.183 --> 00:04:27.415
Here is the station code.

00:04:27.535 --> 00:04:29.599
OurWater made it for you.

00:04:29.719 --> 00:04:35.671
It cannot be changed, because the QR label on the
well and every measurement are tied to this code.

00:04:36.483 --> 00:04:40.923
Edit lets you fix the name or the village
later, but never the code.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:45.038
There was no question about who can see the
station.

00:04:45.158 --> 00:04:48.014
New stations are visible to everyone.

00:04:48.134 --> 00:04:54.182
To keep one private, press Ask to change
privacy here, and a Super Admin will decide.

00:04:54.983 --> 00:04:58.511
Further down, Show QR code makes a label.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.007
Print it and paste it on the well.

00:05:01.127 --> 00:05:03.623
Scanning it opens this station.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:09.730
Back on My stations, the new well is on your
list, ready for its first measurement.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:17.078
That is how to add a station: the kind, the
name, the place, a photo, and a review.

00:05:17.198 --> 00:05:20.102
Next, record its first measurement.

00:05:20.222 --> 00:05:22.886
Thanks for helping look after our water.
